.TH ALERT\-MAILER 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 158367ea" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
alert\-mailer \- Send alert mail for Alertmanager page and ticket routes; the only mailer in the Kingdom (ADR\-100).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alert\-mailer
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send alert mail for Alertmanager page and ticket routes; the only mailer in the Kingdom (ADR\-100).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-addr \fISTRING\fR
listen address (default :19130)
.TP
.B \-\-heartbeat\-addr \fISTRING\fR
heartbeat listen address (used only when HEARTBEAT_HOSTS is set) (default :19131)
.TP
.B \-\-policy \fISTRING\fR
observability/alerting/policy.yaml (default /etc/alert\-mailer/policy.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir \fISTRING\fR
where state.json lives (cap, tickets, outbox) (default /var/lib/alert\-mailer)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH NOTES
Relay settings come from the environment: SMTP_SMARTHOST, SMTP_USERNAME, SMTP_PASSWORD.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
alert\-mailer \-\-policy observability/alerting/policy.yaml
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
